  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "application",
      "stem": "Factorise: 2x^2 + 5x - 3",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "(2x - 1)(x + 3)" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "(2x + 1)(x - 3)" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "(2x + 3)(x - 1)" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "(2x - 3)(x + 1)" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "a",
      "explanation": "ac = 2 x (-3) = -6. Two numbers that multiply to -6 and add to 5: 6 and -1. Split: 2x^2 + 6x - x - 3 = 2x(x + 3) - 1(x + 3) = (2x - 1)(x + 3). Check: (2x - 1)(x + 3) = 2x^2 + 6x - x - 3 = 2x^2 + 5x - 3."
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "application",
      "stem": "Factorise: 6x^2 - 7x - 5",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "(3x + 5)(2x - 1)" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "(3x - 5)(2x + 1)" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "(6x - 5)(x + 1)" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "(2x + 1)(3x - 5)" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "b",
      "explanation": "ac = 6 x (-5) = -30. Numbers: 3 and -10 (multiply to -30, add to -7). Split: 6x^2 + 3x - 10x - 5 = 3x(2x + 1) - 5(2x + 1) = (3x - 5)(2x + 1)."
    },
