      "stem": "Factorise: 9x^2 - 4",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "(3x - 2)^2" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "(9x + 4)(x - 1)" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "(3x + 2)(3x - 2)" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "(3x - 4)(3x + 1)" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "c",
      "explanation": "This is a difference of two squares: (3x)^2 - 2^2 = (3x + 2)(3x - 2)."
    },
    {
      "id": "q4",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "application",
      "stem": "Factorise fully: 4x^2 + 14x + 6",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "(4x + 2)(x + 3)" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "2(2x + 1)(x + 3)" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "(2x + 6)(2x + 1)" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "2(2x + 3)(x + 1)" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "b",
      "explanation": "First take out common factor 2: 2(2x^2 + 7x + 3). Then factorise 2x^2 + 7x + 3: ac = 6, numbers 1 and 6. Split: 2x^2 + x + 6x + 3 = x(2x + 1) + 3(2x + 1) = (2x + 1)(x + 3). Answer: 2(2x + 1)(x + 3)."
    },
